cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DocTrace in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "DocTrace: Document-Image Tampering Localization with JPEG Robustness Analysis"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-10"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/UjwalSanikam/DocTrace"
repository-code: "https://github.com/UjwalSanikam/DocTrace"
authors:
  - family-names: Sanikam
    given-names: Ujwal
keywords:
  - document forensics
  - image tampering detection
  - image segmentation
  - JPEG robustness
  - error level analysis
  - computer vision
  - PyTorch
abstract: >
  DocTrace is a local computer-vision research prototype for per-pixel
  document-image tampering localization. It trains a ResNet-18 U-Net on the
  DocTamper dataset, investigates the effect of JPEG augmentation on
  compression robustness via a controlled matched-training comparison, and
  provides a browser-based inspection interface with Error Level Analysis,
  multi-condition sensitivity probing (jpeg90/70/50 and blur), and
  connected-component region summaries. No novel architecture or
  state-of-the-art result is claimed; the contribution is a reproducible
  robustness comparison, explicit failure analysis, and a transparent local demo.
